-- Q2445: Tax Procedures [medium/L1]
-- Issues: #3
UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (D): Under IRC Section 6601, interest on tax underpayments runs from the due date of the return (without regard to extensions) to the date of payment. Under Section 6622, the interest is compounded daily at the federal short-term rate plus 3 percentage points, adjusted quarterly.
Wrong (A): Personal interest on tax underpayments is not deductible for individual taxpayers under IRC Section 163(h).
Wrong (B): The rate is not a flat 5% — it is the federal short-term rate plus 3 percentage points, adjusted quarterly by the IRS.
Wrong (C): Interest continues to accrue during the period a case is pending in Tax Court; there is no suspension for litigation.$EXPL$
