Wrong (A): Refund offsets do not require a CDP hearing; the IRS may offset refunds against outstanding liabilities without a pre-action hearing.
Wrong (B): A federal tax lien requires post-filing notice within 5 business days under Section 6320, not a pre-filing hearing.
