-- Q2449: Tax Procedures [medium/L2]
-- Issues: #3
UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (A): Under IRC Section 6662(d)(1)(A), a substantial understatement for individuals exists when the understatement exceeds the greater of $5,000 or 10% of the tax required to be shown. Here, 10% of $50,000 equals $5,000, so the threshold is $5,000. Since the $6,000 understatement exceeds $5,000, the 20% accuracy-related penalty applies.
Wrong (B): This choice miscalculates the test. The $6,000 understatement does exceed the greater of $5,000 or $5,000 (10% of $50,000), so a substantial understatement exists.
Wrong (C): The $1,000 threshold has no basis in Section 6662; the correct individual threshold is the greater of $5,000 or 10% of the tax.
