  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (D): Under the Restatement (Second) of Contracts Section 360, specific performance is available when monetary damages are inadequate because the subject matter is unique. Real property is presumed unique under Section 360(b), making specific performance routinely available for land sale contracts.
Wrong (A): Specific performance is not granted for standard commodities available on the open market, because monetary damages can adequately compensate through a substitute purchase.
Wrong (B): The ability to prove dollar damages with certainty actually weighs against specific performance, since adequate monetary relief is available.
