  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (A): Under UCC Section 2-201(2), between merchants, a written confirmation sufficient against the sender also satisfies the Statute of Frauds against the recipient if the recipient does not object in writing within 10 days. Baxter''s failure to object binds the merchant as if it had signed the confirmation.
Wrong (B): The merchant exception under Section 2-201(2) specifically eliminates the requirement for the recipient''s own signature between merchants.
Wrong (C): The objection period is 10 days from receipt of the confirmation, not three years. The statute of limitations is a separate concept.
Wrong (D): There is no penalty for failing to respond. The consequence is that the confirmation satisfies the Statute of Frauds against the non-responding merchant.$EXPL$
