-- Q2473: Business Law: Contracts [medium/L1]
-- Issues: #3
UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (D): Under the Restatement (Second) of Contracts Section 376, rescission cancels the contract and requires mutual restitution, restoring both parties to their pre-contract positions. This equitable remedy is available for fraud, material misrepresentation, mutual mistake, duress, or failure of consideration.
Wrong (A): Rescission does not require a finding of criminal fraud. Civil misrepresentation, as in Stratton''s case, is sufficient to support rescission.
Wrong (B): Rescission restores parties to pre-contract positions through restitution — it does not award double the contract value or punitive multiples.
